Subject: [PATCH] linux-dmabuf: implement per-surface feedback

The zwp_linux_dmabuf_v1 global is created at version 4, which covers both
get_default_feedback and get_surface_feedback. Only the former creates a
resource; the latter is a stub that returns without touching the id the client
just allocated.

Mesa 25.2 and newer request per-surface feedback. Mesa keeps the proxy and
destroys it when the surface goes away, at which point libwayland-server cannot
resolve the id and posts wl_display.error(invalid object), which is fatal for
the connection -- not just for that object. The next view target initialising on
the same connection binds no wl_compositor and WS::BaseTarget::initialize()
calls g_error(), aborting the web process:

    wl_display#1: error 0: invalid object 12
    (WPEWebProcess:497): WPE-FDO-ERROR **: Failed to bind wl_compositor

On a Raspberry Pi CM4 with Cog 0.18.5, WPE WebKit 2.50.5 and Mesa 26.1.2 the web
process died on every third cross-site navigation.

Answer per-surface feedback with the default feedback's tranches. The protocol
permits it: per-surface feedback is an optimisation hint, and a client that gets
the default tranches is still correct.

See docs/wpe-fdo-surface-feedback-crash.md in the chromasurf monorepo for the
full protocol trace, and https://github.com/Igalia/cog/issues/774 for the
related boot-time crash from the same Mesa change.

---
 src/linux-dmabuf/linux-dmabuf.cpp | 11 +++++++----
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

--- a/src/linux-dmabuf/linux-dmabuf.cpp
+++ b/src/linux-dmabuf/linux-dmabuf.cpp
@@ -396,12 +396,15 @@
 }
 
 static void
-linux_dmabuf_get_surface_feedback(struct wl_client*,
-                                  struct wl_resource*,
-                                  uint32_t /* dmabuf_feedback_id */,
+linux_dmabuf_get_surface_feedback(struct wl_client *client,
+                                  struct wl_resource *dmabuf_resource,
+                                  uint32_t dmabuf_feedback_id,
                                   struct wl_resource*)
 {
-    // We don't support per surface feedback, but since we claim to support version 4 we need to provide an implementation.
+    // No surface-specific tranches to offer, but the resource has to exist: the
+    // client destroys it on surface teardown, and an unknown object id makes
+    // libwayland fail the whole connection.
+    linux_dmabuf_get_default_feedback(client, dmabuf_resource, dmabuf_feedback_id);
 }
 
 static const struct zwp_linux_dmabuf_v1_interface linux_dmabuf_implementation = {
